    "needs_human": false,
    "human_action": "",
    "clause": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions",
    "note": "Bind all pairs before timing; sample at each interval and the exact endpoint, including a partial final interval. Monitor unbound outputs too; only bound streams owe traffic. Teardown after the final snapshot.",
    "assert_clauses": {
      "release.complete-evidence": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions: all required assertions need measured PASS records on the exact image; missing, SKIP, INFO, KNOWN-PENDING, NEEDS-HUMAN and INSTRUMENT-SUSPECT cannot qualify a release",
      "soak.continuous-duration": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions: at least 604800 continuous seconds after all pairs flow; no concatenating interrupted runs or counting setup time",
      "soak.bound-both-directions": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions: keep the compatible AAF and CRF pairs bound and flowing in both directions throughout the observation window",
      "soak.counter-walk": "Milan v1.2 Table 5.4 / Table 5.6; REQ-VER-06: read every declared input and output, CRF included, at baseline, each interval and the endpoint; validate masks and lock/start-stop invariants; no unexplained counter reset",
      "soak.no-counter-errors": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions; Milan v1.2 5.3.8.10 Table 5.6; IEEE 1722-2016 4.4.4.6: zero SEQ_NUM_MISMATCH and STREAM_INTERRUPTED growth; no unexplained MEDIA_UNLOCKED; record every delta and each unlock explanation",
      "soak.gptp-continuity": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions; Milan v1.2 4.2.6.2.4: coherent fabric publication reads and transition evidence prove no asCapable loss",
      "soak.tu-within-holdover": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions; Milan v1.2 Annex B.1/B.1.1 / IEEE 1722-2016 4.4.4.7: each tu interval contains at least one recorded discontinuity: PHC settime/adjtime, fabric discontinuity, or GM-identity edge; containment uses [observed_start - observation_resolution_s, clear); measure from the last recorded discontinuity before tu clears; it clears within 0.5 s plus the stated observation resolution; uncorrelated tu fails; resolution comes from wire capture and correlated event timestamps; it includes launch-to-capture latency and event-to-capture correlation error; B.1.1 states 0.25 s, read by the project as a minimum; clock validity implements 0.25-0.5 s; B.1's 5 s media-clock holdover is not a tu bound; periodic healthy samples alone cannot prove this",
      "soak.timestamp-margin": "docs/reference/REGISTER_MAP.md AVTPRX_TSD (0x6EC): record signed ns presentation margin for the last accepted STREAM_INPUT[0] PDU, with freshness evidence; never attribute this single-index register to other streams",
      "soak.uptime-monotonic": "REQUIREMENTS.md REQ-VER-06; issue #396 owner/assignment decisions: DUT uptime advances monotonically; reboot or unavailable uptime evidence cannot pass the continuous soak"
    },
    "assert_severity": {
      "release.complete-evidence": "SHALL",
